cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying article."
title: "SPHINX: Spatial Proteomic inference from Histology with Integrated Neighborhood conteXt"
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
abstract: >-
  SPHINX predicts multiplex protein expression, cell identity and spatial tissue
  organisation from routine H&E whole-slide images at single-cell resolution.
  The model combines a dual-scale vision transformer encoder, a biology-prior
  graph attention module, a spatial neighbourhood graph attention module and a
  router-multi-gate fusion. Downstream modules provide pseudo-multiplex image
  rendering, spatial niche analysis (TIL / TLS / CAF) and immune hot/cold
  tumour phenotyping.
